# [[.Name]]

An [Astrona](https://cli.astrona.io) lab with two kind clusters side by side: the lab's own, and **backend** (`runtime.kind.labs` in `config.yaml`) — a service published as NodePort 30080.

```
config.yaml
docs/                      # student docs
solution/                  # the lab's own reference solution (astrona test)
labs/backend/bootstrap/    # sets up the backend cluster
labs/backend/testing/      # the backend cluster's part of the reference solution
```

```sh
astrona run -c .            # creates backend, then the lab
astrona docs question       # read the task
astrona submit --watch      # live feedback while you work
astrona submit              # grades both clusters (checks with cluster: backend)
astrona destroy -c .        # removes both
```

Authoring: `astrona validate -c .` checks the config; `astrona test -c .` creates test copies of both clusters and proves the reference solution (`solution/` and `labs/backend/testing/`) passes every check. `.github/workflows/lab.yml` runs both on every pull request.

Guide: https://cli.astrona.io/guides/linked-labs/
